@startuml
actor "Jupyter Notebook" as JN
participant "RunPod API" as API
participant "Container" as Container
participant "SSH Server" as SSH
participant "Ollama + LM-Eval" as EVAL
participant "GPU" as GPU

== Pod Creation ==
JN -> API: create_pod(config)
API -> Container: provision instance
Container -> GPU: allocate resources
API --> JN: return pod_id, SSH endpoint

== Pod Status Polling ==
JN -> API: get_pod(pod_id)
API -> Container: check status
Container --> API: RUNNING + SSH ready
API --> JN: pod details

== SSH Connection & Provisioning ==
JN -> SSH: SSH connect (with key)
SSH --> JN: authenticated
JN -> SSH: install Ollama
JN -> SSH: start ollama serve
JN -> SSH: install lm_eval
JN -> SSH: ollama pull model
SSH -> GPU: download model to VRAM

== Upload Configuration ==
JN -> SSH: upload task YAML files
SSH --> JN: configs stored

== Run Evaluation ==
JN -> SSH: execute lm_eval command
SSH -> EVAL: start evaluation
EVAL -> EVAL: load task config
loop For each test case
    EVAL -> GPU: inference request
    GPU --> EVAL: model response
end
EVAL -> Container: write results.json
EVAL -> Container: write samples.jsonl
EVAL --> SSH: evaluation complete
SSH --> JN: command finished

== Download Results ==
JN -> SSH: SFTP download request
SSH -> Container: read output files
Container --> SSH: results + samples
SSH --> JN: transfer files

== Cleanup ==
JN -> API: terminate_pod(pod_id)
API -> Container: destroy instance
Container -> GPU: release resources
API --> JN: pod terminated

@enduml